---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../config/site";

const prose = "max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600";
const sectionHeading =
  "text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-3xl";

// Capability groups mirror the homepage's Core Focus areas, plus the
// systems/security foundations underneath them. Some groups need more
// than one paragraph, so each carries its own list.
const capabilityGroups = [
  {
    title: "Production Operations & Reliability",
    paragraphs: [
      "Production operations and ownership, incident investigation and root-cause analysis, monitoring and alerting design, release readiness and release operations, and troubleshooting across application, API and database layers.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Automation & Data Systems",
    paragraphs: [
      "SQL and PostgreSQL, Python and JavaScript automation, MongoDB, Snowflake, Redis, Prefect-orchestrated ETL and production pipelines, data-quality frameworks and validation, REST API testing with Postman, and operational tooling and dashboards in Retool.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Cloud & Infrastructure",
    paragraphs: [
      "AWS, Docker, Kubernetes and EKS, Terraform, ECR, GitHub Actions CI/CD, and Prometheus and Grafana monitoring — together with the DevSecOps practices that go with them: vulnerability gates, hardened container runtimes and scoped access. This is where my project work has been concentrated, and the case studies go into the decisions in detail.",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "Systems & Security Foundations",
    paragraphs: [
      "Professionally, I have run identity and access operations through JumpCloud: user lifecycle, groups, permissions and RBAC, onboarding and offboarding, and internal system access administration.",
      "Underneath that sits broader training in Linux administration, networking, systems administration and cyber security — the background I rely on when a problem sits below the application layer.",
    ],
  },
] as const;

const technicalTraining = [
  "Linux administration",
  "Network administration (CCNA curriculum)",
  "Microsoft systems administration (MCSA curriculum)",
  "Cyber security",
  "SOC fundamentals and operations",
  "Firewall and network security fundamentals",
  "DevSecOps",
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${siteConfig.name}`}
  description="Technical Operations background across production reliability, automation, data systems and cloud infrastructure — plus how I work and what I've been building."
>
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">
    About
  </h1>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
    <p class={prose}>
      I work in Technical Operations. Most of my professional experience is in
      production: how systems behave under real load, why they fail, and what it
      takes to keep them dependable while the business keeps changing them.
    </p>
    <p class={prose}>
      That work has been hands-on throughout — querying production databases to
      understand what actually happened, validating releases before they ship,
      and building the monitoring that surfaces a problem while it still
      matters.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Professional progression -->
  <section aria-labelledby="progression-heading" class="mt-20">
    <h2 id="progression-heading" class={sectionHeading}>
      Professional progression
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        I started at YuviTal as a TechOps Engineer, working hands-on across
        production and staging: backend and database testing, SQL and NoSQL
        investigation, validating ETL and data flows, checking API-based
        integrations, and tracking defects through to resolution with the
        developers who fixed them. A good deal of it was investigation,
        including fraud and abuse analysis in production data and the hardening
        work that followed.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        As TechOps Team Lead the scope widened from investigating problems to
        preventing them. I built monitoring and automated alerting across
        production services and pipelines, wrote automated data-quality controls
        in SQL and Python across Prefect-orchestrated pipelines supporting more
        than 100 production tables, and took ownership of release readiness and
        validation. The role also covered identity and access administration
        through JumpCloud, and operational tooling built in Retool.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        I led a three-person technical team — one developer and two TechOps
        engineers — while staying hands-on with the systems myself, and worked
        directly with engineering, product, business stakeholders, vendors and
        B2B and B2C clients on technical delivery.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        More recently I have been building the infrastructure side end to end:
        AWS environments provisioned with Terraform, Kubernetes workloads, CI/CD
        pipelines, monitoring, and the delivery and teardown automation around
        them. The projects on this site are where that work lives.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Capabilities -->
  <section aria-labelledby="capabilities-heading" class="mt-20">
    <h2 id="capabilities-heading" class={sectionHeading}>Capabilities</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        capabilityGroups.map((group) => (
          <div class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">{group.title}</h3>
            <div class="mt-3 space-y-3">
              {group.paragraphs.map((paragraph) => (
                <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
                  {paragraph}
                </p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How I work -->
  <section aria-labelledby="how-i-work-heading" class="mt-20">
    <h2 id="how-i-work-heading" class={sectionHeading}>How I work</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
      <p class={prose}>
        Hands-on first. Leading a team never meant stopping doing the work; it
        meant being responsible for more of it, and making sure the people
        around me could move faster than they could alone.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        I prefer to fix the class of problem rather than the instance. If the
        same incident keeps arriving, the useful work is usually removing the
        conditions that allow it rather than closing it faster. Most of the
        outcomes I'm satisfied with came from turning a recurring manual problem
        into an automated control.
      </p>
      <p class={prose}>
        I work across boundaries regularly — with engineering, product, business
        stakeholders, vendors and clients. Operations sits between all of them,
        so a large part of the role is making technical constraints legible to
        people who don't work in them, and the reverse.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Technical training -->
  <section aria-labelledby="training-heading" class="mt-20">
    <h2 id="training-heading" class={sectionHeading}>Technical training</h2>
    <p class={`mt-4 ${prose}`}>
      Completed training programs covering the systems and security foundations
      behind operations work:
    </p>
    <ul
      class="mt-4 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-base text-slate-600"
    >
      {technicalTraining.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Closing -->
  <section aria-labelledby="closing-heading" class="mt-20">
    <h2 id="closing-heading" class="sr-only">Where to go next</h2>
    <p class={prose}>
      The <a
        href="/projects/"
        class="rounded font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-slate-900"
        >projects</a
      > go into the engineering decisions in more detail, and the <a
        href="/experience/"
        class="rounded font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-slate-900"
        >experience</a
      > page covers the professional work. If you want to talk about any of it, my
      details are in the footer.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
